      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:2:2:3",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا الْحَسَنِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنْ أَدْنَى مَا يَكُونُ مِنَ الْحَيْضِ فَقَالَ أَدْنَاهُ ثَلَاثَةٌ وَ أَبْعَدُهُ عَشَرَةٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Ismail, from Al Fazl Bin Shazaan and Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, altogether from Safwan Bin Yahya who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> about the least of what the menstruation (<span class=\"iTxt\">Haydh</span>) can happen to be. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The least is for three days, and the furthest (it can go to) is ten (days)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Muhammad ibn ’Isma‘il has narrated from al-Fadl ibn Shadhan and Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father all from Safwan ibn Yahya who has said the following: “I once asked abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the minimum duration of Hayd (menses). He (the Imam) said, ‘Its minimum is three days and the longest is ten days.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
